From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:53:27 -0400
Subject: feat: a drag takes a tab into the essentials and out (issue 16)

As in Arc (pins H27; BACKLOG S-277, GitHub issue 16): a tab's row
dragged over the essentials, or the room above the Space's title down to
the list, lights the essentials, and released there it becomes an
essential, before the card it was dropped on or after the last. An
essential's card dragged onto the list shows the bar between the rows
where it will land, and released there it stops being an essential, at
that place: under the Clear line a tab, over it a pin of the Space. It had
taken the tab's menu. The drop decides, as a drop across the Clear line
does (pins H14): TabDragHandlerImpl keeps the pointer's last place,
PinnedTabContainerView lights for it, and UnpinnedTabContainerView says
where a row brought into the list would go.

Tests: PinnedRunTest.ADragTakesATabIntoTheEssentialsAndOut.

Why: Arc users move tabs into and out of their Favorites by dragging, and
asked for it (GitHub issue 16).
Removable when: never; it is product behaviour.
